      "id": 301,
      "options": {
        "content": "### Top Bottlenecks & Automated Suggested Actions\n\n| Rank | Stage | Primary Cause | Recommended Serving Action |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **1** | **`prefill`** | High prompt length / quadratic attention | Enable chunked prefill (`--enable-chunked-prefill`), activate prefix caching (`--enable-prefix-caching`), scale tensor parallelism. |\n| **2** | **`decode`** | Autoregressive memory bandwidth saturation | Enable speculative decoding, optimize KV cache block size, reduce max output tokens. |\n| **3** | **`queue_wait`** | High arrival rate exceeding scheduling capacity | Increase concurrency limit (`--max-num-seqs`), scale replicas, optimize KV cache memory allocation. |\n| **4** | **`tokenization`** | CPU string encoding serialization | Switch to fast Rust-based HuggingFace tokenizer, cache tokenized prompts on client/worker. |\n| **5** | **`network`** | Client-server transmission latency / jitter | Colocate client and server in same subnet, enable persistent HTTP keep-alive, switch to gRPC. |\n\n*Evaluated by Member 4 `BottleneckAnalyzer` using offline request traces and Prometheus real-time histograms.*",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "title": "Bottleneck Remediation Reference Matrix",
